# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
# 
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
# 
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD p63869-1 63869 black
ADD p60483-2 60483 lightgray
WHY Aligns the grey two-hole beam beside the cross bore of the black triple connector so the next step can capture them with the axle.

STEP 2
ADD p4519-1 4519 lightgray
ADD p87082-1 87082 black
CONNECT p4519-1.axle2 -> p63869-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p4519-1.axle3 -> p60483-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p87082-1.pin1 -> p60483-2.hole1 STIFF
WHY Slides the three-length axle through the aligned cross holes and places one pin of the black hub in the grey beam's round hole.

STEP 3
ADD p60483-1 60483 lightgray
CONNECT p4519-1.axle1 -> p60483-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p87082-1.pin2 -> p60483-1.hole1 STIFF
WHY Closes the other side with the second grey beam, capturing the remaining cross shaft and the hub's other pin.

STEP 4
ADD p64179-1 64179 lightgray
ADD p2780-1 2780 black
ADD p2780-2 2780 black
CONNECT p2780-1.pin1 -> p63869-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT p2780-2.pin1 -> p63869-1.hole3 STIFF
CONNECT p2780-1.pin2 -> p64179-1.hole4 STIFF
CONNECT p2780-2.pin2 -> p64179-1.hole2 STIFF
WHY Pins the connector block to the short side of the rectangular frame with the two black pins two holes apart.

STEP 5
ADD p6558-1 6558 blue
ADD p6558-2 6558 blue
CONNECT p6558-1.pin2 -> p64179-1.hole5 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-2.pin2 -> p64179-1.hole1 STIFF
WHY Inserts the two long blue pins through the frame corners with their ends projecting above and below for the next layers.

STEP 6
GROUP upper-front-crossbar
ADD p22961-1 22961 lightgray
ADD p22961-2 22961 lightgray
ADD p32034-1 32034 darkgray
CONNECT p22961-1.axle1 -> p32034-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p22961-2.axle1 -> p32034-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
END
ATTACH upper-front-crossbar
CONNECT p6558-1.pin1 -> p22961-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-2.pin1 -> p22961-2.hole1 STIFF
WHY Joins the two grey axle-pin hubs with the straight grey cross connector and fits their round holes over the blue corner pins.

STEP 7
GROUP bevel-input-support
ADD p15462-1 15462 brown
ADD p6589-1 6589 tan
ADD p48496-1 48496 black
CONNECT p15462-1.axle5 -> p6589-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p15462-1.axle5 -> p48496-1.hole2 TURNS
END
ATTACH bevel-input-support
CONNECT p15462-1.axle4 -> p64179-1.hole3 TURNS
CONNECT p15462-1.axle3 -> p63869-1.hole2 TURNS
CONNECT p48496-1.pin1 -> p32034-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT p48496-1.pin2 -> p87082-1.hole1 STIFF
WHY Feeds the brown stopped axle through the front bearings and pins the black toggle support in place, keeping the tan bevel gear locked to the rotating axle.

STEP 8
ADD p32270-1 32270 black
CONNECT p15462-1.axle2 -> p32270-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Adds the black twelve-tooth double-bevel gear to the exposed front end of the same brown axle.

STEP 9
ADD p99008-1 99008 tan
ADD p6589-2 6589 tan
ADD p59443-1 59443 yellow
CONNECT p99008-1.axle3 -> p59443-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p99008-1.axle1 -> p6589-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p99008-1.axle2 -> p48496-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT p99008-1.axle1 -> p48496-1.hole3 TURNS
MESH p6589-1.teeth p6589-2.teeth
RATIO p6589-1 p6589-2 1/1
WHY Installs the vertical tan axle with its yellow extension and meshes the two twelve-tooth bevel gears at right angles inside the black support.

STEP 10
ADD p41239-1 41239 darkgray
ADD p41239-2 41239 darkgray
ADD p6558-3 6558 blue
ADD p6558-4 6558 blue
CONNECT p6558-3.pin2 -> p41239-1.hole13 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-4.pin2 -> p41239-2.hole13 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-3.pin1 -> p64179-1.hole8 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-4.pin1 -> p64179-1.hole9 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-2.pin3 -> p41239-1.hole11 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-1.pin3 -> p41239-2.hole11 STIFF
WHY Adds the two long side rails beneath the frame, using the existing corner pins and the new pins two holes farther along each rail.

STEP 11
GROUP lower-axle-frame
ADD p64179-2 64179 lightgray
ADD p2780-3 2780 black
ADD p2780-4 2780 black
ADD p55013-1 55013 darkgray
ADD p6589-3 6589 tan
ADD p3713-1 3713 red
ADD p62462-1 62462 red
CONNECT p2780-3.pin1 -> p64179-2.hole10 STIFF
CONNECT p2780-4.pin2 -> p64179-2.hole11 STIFF
CONNECT p55013-1.axle8 -> p64179-2.hole18 TURNS
CONNECT p55013-1.axle2 -> p64179-2.hole3 TURNS
CONNECT p55013-1.axle6 -> p6589-3.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p55013-1.axle3 -> p3713-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p55013-1.axle4 -> p62462-1.hole1 TURNS
END
ATTACH lower-axle-frame
CONNECT p6558-3.pin3 -> p64179-2.hole8 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-4.pin3 -> p64179-2.hole9 STIFF
MESH p6589-3.teeth p6589-2.teeth
RATIO p6589-3 p6589-2 1/1
WHY Builds the lower frame around the stopped eight-length axle with its red sleeve and bush, then stacks it beneath the rails so its bevel gear meets the vertical gear.

STEP 12
ADD p6558-5 6558 blue
ADD p6558-6 6558 blue
ADD p6558-7 6558 blue
ADD p6558-8 6558 blue
CONNECT p6558-5.pin2 -> p41239-2.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-6.pin2 -> p41239-1.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-7.pin2 -> p41239-1.hole8 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-8.pin2 -> p41239-2.hole8 STIFF
WHY Places four long blue pins through the forward portions of the rails to hold the next rectangular frame.

STEP 13
ADD p64178-1 64178 lightgray
CONNECT p15462-1.axle1 -> p64178-1.hole22 TURNS
WHY Lowers the large frame between the rails, feeding the exposed brown axle into the central round hole of its rear crossbar.

STEP 14
CONNECT p6558-5.pin3 -> p64178-1.hole5 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-6.pin3 -> p64178-1.hole9 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-7.pin3 -> p64178-1.hole24 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-8.pin3 -> p64178-1.hole20 STIFF
WHY Pushes the four waiting blue pins up into the large frame to hold it square on both rails.

STEP 15
GROUP turntable
ADD p18939-1 18939 lightgray
ADD p18938-1 18938 black
ADD p32054-1 32054 black
ADD p32054-2 32054 black
CONNECT p18938-1.? -> p18939-1.? TURNS
CONNECT p32054-1.pin1 -> p18939-1.hole6 STIFF
CONNECT p32054-2.pin1 -> p18939-1.hole4 STIFF
END
ATTACH turntable
CONNECT p32054-1.pin2 -> p64178-1.hole21 STIFF
CONNECT p32054-2.pin2 -> p64178-1.hole23 STIFF
WHY Snaps the black toothed turntable into its grey base and pins one base bracket to the large frame, leaving the black ring free to rotate.

STEP 16
ADD p32054-3 32054 black
ADD p32054-4 32054 black
CONNECT p32054-3.pin1 -> p64178-1.hole6 STIFF
CONNECT p32054-4.pin1 -> p64178-1.hole8 STIFF
CONNECT p32054-3.pin2 -> p18939-1.hole3 STIFF
CONNECT p32054-4.pin2 -> p18939-1.hole1 STIFF
MESH p32270-1.teeth p18938-1.teeth
RATIO p32270-1 p18938-1 1/5
WHY Pins the other turntable bracket to the frame and checks that turning the yellow input drives the black ring through the twelve-tooth pinion.

STEP 17
GROUP actuator-carrier
ADD p64178-2 64178 lightgray
ADD p2780-5 2780 black
ADD p2780-6 2780 black
CONNECT p2780-5.pin1 -> p64178-2.hole4 STIFF
CONNECT p2780-6.pin2 -> p64178-2.hole3 STIFF
WHY Starts the lower actuator carrier with two black pins projecting from opposite sides near its open end.

STEP 18
ADD p60485-1 60485 lightgray
ADD p59443-2 59443 yellow
ADD p6589-4 6589 tan
CONNECT p60485-1.axle9 -> p59443-2.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT p60485-1.axle8 -> p64178-2.hole22 TURNS
CONNECT p60485-1.axle2 -> p64178-2.hole7 TURNS
CONNECT p60485-1.axle1 -> p6589-4.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Threads the nine-length axle through both carrier crossbars and locks the tan bevel gear and yellow connector to its opposite ends.

STEP 19
ADD lift-actuator 92693 lightgray
ADD p44294-1 44294 yellow
ADD p6589-5 6589 tan
ADD p3713-2 3713 red
CONNECT p6589-5.axlehole1 -> lift-actuator.? LOCKED
CONNECT p44294-1.axle2 -> p64178-2.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT p44294-1.axle6 -> p64178-2.hole2 TURNS
CONNECT p44294-1.axle3~ -> lift-actuator.? TURNS
CONNECT p44294-1.axle3 -> p3713-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Sets the small actuator to the pictured extension, adds its tan input gear, and captures its mounting fork on the yellow axle with the red bush beside it.

STEP 20
ADD p87407-1 87407 lightgray
CONNECT p44294-1.axle4 -> p87407-1.hole1 TURNS
MESH p87407-1.teeth p6589-5.teeth
RATIO p87407-1 p6589-5 5/3
MESH p6589-4.teeth p87407-1.teeth
RATIO p6589-4 p87407-1 3/5
WHY Slides the yellow axle through the free twenty-tooth gear so it transfers rotation from the carrier shaft to the actuator input while remaining free on the pivot axle.
END

STEP 21
ATTACH actuator-carrier
CONNECT p6558-5.pin1 -> p64178-2.hole5 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-6.pin1 -> p64178-2.hole9 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-7.pin1 -> p64178-2.hole24 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-8.pin1 -> p64178-2.hole20 STIFF
CONNECT p55013-1.axle1 -> p59443-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Fits the actuator carrier beneath the rails and joins its nine-length shaft to the stopped axle with the yellow connector, then checks that pushing the rear axle turns the actuator drive.

STEP 22
GROUP upper-bevel-crank
ADD p4519-4 4519 lightgray
ADD p18575-1 18575 tan
ADD p32034-2 32034 darkgray
ADD p59443-3 59443 yellow
CONNECT p4519-4.axle3 -> p18575-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT p4519-4.axle2 -> p32034-2.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT p4519-4.axle1 -> p59443-3.axlehole1 LOCKED
END
ATTACH upper-bevel-crank
MESH p18575-1.teeth p6589-3.teeth
RATIO p6589-3 p18575-1 3/5
WHY Places the second yellow input above the tan twenty-tooth gear and the straight grey bearing bar, meshing that gear with the lower axle's bevel gear.

STEP 23
ADD p4519-2 4519 lightgray
ADD p4519-3 4519 lightgray
CONNECT p4519-2.axle2 -> p64179-1.hole14 TURNS
CONNECT p4519-3.axle2 -> p64179-1.hole15 TURNS
CONNECT p4519-2.axle1 -> p32034-2.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT p4519-3.axle3 -> p32034-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Secures the straight bearing bar between the frame sides with the two grey three-length axles, leaving its central vertical input free to turn.
